Summarise an archive: its format chain, entry counts, sizes and compression ratio, methods,
encryption, whether it is solid or self-extracting, and its comment.

Usage: beezip info [OPTIONS] <ARCHIVE>

Arguments:
  <ARCHIVE>
          The archive

Options:
  -p, --password <PASSWORD>
          The password, if entry names or data need one

      --name-encoding <ENCODING>
          How names stored as bytes are read: zip names without the UTF-8 flag, tar names outside
          pax records, cpio, ar, LHA, ARJ, ACE, ZOO, ARC and squashfs names, CAB names without the
          UTF-8 flag, ISO names outside Joliet [default: from config, `auto`]
          
          [possible values: auto, utf-8, cp437, cp850, cp852, cp866, cp874, cp932, cp936, cp949,
          cp950, cp1250, cp1251, cp1252, cp1253, cp1254, cp1255, cp1256, cp1257, cp1258, koi8-r,
          koi8-u, iso-8859-1, iso-8859-2, iso-8859-5, iso-8859-7, euc-jp, gb18030]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --output <FORMAT>
          How to print results; ndjson streams every job event

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   One JSON document on stdout: the output, or `{"error": {...}}`
          - ndjson: Every job event as a JSON line on stdout, ending with `Finished`, `Failed` or
            `Cancelled`
          
          [default: human]

  -q, --quiet
          No progress bars or info messages; warnings still print
